NOTICE

The original PARSHL program (1985, SAIL) reproduced in `original_source/`
and the algorithms it implements are the work of Julius O. Smith III
(CCRMA, Stanford University, https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/). In 2026
the original author released the PARSHL software he wrote under the MIT
License and authorised its inclusion in this repository. This C++20 port
and its extensions are released under the same MIT License by Guillermo
Luis Perna. This work was reviewed and validated by Julius Orion Smith III
(2026).

Reference paper:
  J.O. Smith III & X. Serra, "PARSHL: An Analysis/Synthesis Program for
  Non-Harmonic Sounds Based on a Sinusoidal Representation", Proceedings
  of the International Computer Music Conference (ICMC-87), 1987.
  Also published as CCRMA Technical Report STAN-M-43; reprinted in
  Computer Music Journal, 14(4), 1990.
  https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/parshl/
